  :project agentic-systems

  |title Sample more, and be curious first, before you fixate

  |quote
    I recommend not fixating on the areas you want to engage carefully until you have sampled more and allowed yourself to just be curious first. There is plenty of context remaining.

  |occasion
    Re-opening a de-novo audit of the whole framework, to an agent that had started
    narrowing onto the areas it meant to examine carefully.

  |about
    The anti-premature-convergence move stated as a *sampling* claim rather than a
    thoroughness one: the areas worth careful engagement are not knowable until enough
    has been sampled, so early fixation selects the audit's findings before the audit
    runs. The second sentence removes the only honest excuse for fixating early.

  |before-acting
    - You are choosing what to examine closely before you have surveyed the whole.
    - You are narrowing an investigation to feel like you are making progress.
    - You are budgeting context and treating breadth as the thing to cut.

  |see
    - #exm-diffuse-and-curious-state
    - #exm-burden-of-proof-on-the-reviewer

